From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] KernelSU: hook: include <linux/sched/task_stack.h> unconditionally

kernel/hook/syscall_hook_manager.c gated #include <linux/sched/task_stack.h> on
LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6, 7, 0), leaving task_stack_page()
undeclared when expanding task_pt_regs(current) on newer mainline kernels.
Include <linux/sched/task_stack.h> unconditionally.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff --git a/kernel/hook/syscall_hook_manager.c b/kernel/hook/syscall_hook_manager.c
--- a/kernel/hook/syscall_hook_manager.c
+++ b/kernel/hook/syscall_hook_manager.c
@@ -10,8 +10,8 @@
 #include <linux/version.h>
 #if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6, 7, 0)
 #include <linux/compat.h>
-#include <linux/sched/task_stack.h>
 #endif
+#include <linux/sched/task_stack.h>

 #include "arch.h"
 #include "klog.h" // IWYU pragma: keep
